Author: Jarod Castillo <43973221+Smotto@users.noreply.github.com>
Date:   Sun Nov 1 20:05:42 2026 +0000

    psi: project data requires onto the selected case for guard narrowing (#1276)
    
    Since #958 moved case-local `where` clauses into the data default-domain
    `requires` as `self in Data::Case` disjunctions, a case's own fact span is
    empty except for generic-synthesis impossibility witnesses. The arithmetic
    guard-narrowing step that supplies a selected case's facts at a match arm
    read only that span, so an arm's payload carried no interval. The structural
    judge still projected the disjunction, which is why a callee with
    `ensures result >= 40 && result <= 80` checked, but a callee with no contract
    returned an unbounded `u64`: on 6e5131c510b, 8 of the 10
    four_variant_enum_payload_bound programs were refused (every place whose
    extractor has no `ensures`), and their twins rejected only because the
    positives did.
    
    One owner, `default_domains::selected_case_requirements`, now derives the
    conjuncts the data `requires` implies for one selected case: a clause that
    mentions case membership keeps the single disjunct not refuted by the
    selected case; a clause leaving two live disjuncts, or mentioning no case,
    contributes nothing. Cases are identified by member position so generic
    instances share their template's facts. Guard narrowing reads that list and
    maps `self.field` onto the dispatched place. Rejected: rebuilding the bound
    for call results only, or requiring authors to restate it with `ensures`.
    
    On macos_arm64 with an optimized producer, omega run --both exits 0 in both
    engines for all 10 four programs and all 10 five programs (control); all 18
    twins reject with their fragments. The call_result twin's fragment moves from
    statement 6 to 7: the base refused valid arms as well, the candidate refuses
    only Gamma's weakened arm. The target_body twin pins the current
    `X86TargetProbe::target_probe` / `ArmTargetProbe::target_probe` spelling; its
    obligation is unchanged. The 18 four corpus rows are re-recorded. A 119-fixture
    corpus selection (four, five, match_join_multi_variant_bound,
    case_payload_transport, case_dependent_default_domain and the guarded or
    borrowed case-payload fixtures) shows 32 structural moves against stale
    golden rows; base and candidate produce the same outcome on the 12
    examined, and the 2 std-importing timeouts check with a 900 s cap at load 54.
    
    Still reading the case span: payload interval readers for representation and
    borrowed write-back (`case_where_field_intervals`), payload-write invariant
    windows, totality formation and zero gating.
    
    Co-authored-by: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>

